    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p31.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Modulo \\(x^2+2x+5,\\) we have \\(x^2=-2x-5.\\) Then \\[ x^3=10-x,\\qquad x^4=12x+5. \\] Thus \\[ \\begin{gathered} x^4+px^2+q\\\\ {}\\equiv(12-2p)x+(5-5p+q). \\end{gathered} \\] Both coefficients vanish when \\(p=6\\) and \\(q=25.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Work modulo \\(x^2+2x+5,\\) so \\(x^2=-2x-5\\)",
        "Reduce \\(x^4\\) to a linear expression and make both remainder coefficients zero"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
